<a2ui>
$/={comparison_data:[{Factor:"Curriculum",CBSE:"Built around NCERT and a structured concept-based syllabus; it is widely aligned with Indian competitive exams such as JEE NEET, NEET CUET.",CISCE:"A broader, content-rich syllabus with strong language depth and separate treatment of subjects such as History/Civics Geography from middle school onward.",IB:"-based, concept-led, and interdisciplinary with programmes such as MYP and DP designed around global-minded learning."},{Factor:"Assessment",CBSE:"More exam-led, with longer papers and many question types covering recall, understanding, application, and evaluation.",CISCE:"Exam-heavy but typically more descriptive and detailed with required external and internal.",IB:"Uses a mix of internal and external assessment; MYP external assessment is optional and DP adds essays, projects, and other coursework-heavy elements."},{Factor:"Subject flexibility",CBSE:"Generally more structured with fewer combinations than international curricula.",CISCE:"Moderate flexibility but still more fixed than IB.",IB:"Greater flexibility, especially in subject choice and in how learners connect disciplines."},{Factor:"Transferability",CBSE:"Transfers most cleanly between schools within India; CBSE also also has broadest domestic footprint.",CISCE:"Transfers best within CISCE schools but the smaller school network can make moves less convenient than CBSE.",IB:"Best when moving between international schools; recognition is global, but local can depend on school level and mapping."}],questions:[{id:"1",text:"Which programme do you actually offer at secondary level: CBSE, ICSE/ISC, or IB?",type:"text"},{id:"2",text:"How many subject combinations are available in Classes 9–1–12, and can students change them later?",type:"text"},{id:"3",text:"What proportion of marks comes from board exams, internal assessment, projects, practicals and coursework?",type:"text"},{id:"4",text:"How do you support students who may transfer to another school or board in future?",type:"text"},{id:"5",text:"For IB schools, which subjects are offered in the school, and how they align with university goals?",type:"text"},{id:"6",text:"For CBSE or CISCE schools, how do you do you balance board with deeper learning and deeper learning stress management?",type:"text"},{id:"7",text:"What are the class sizes, teacher qualifications, resources, and language support for the secondary years?",type:"text"}]
=Column(3)
Tabs(Tabs(activeTab={:"1","2","3","4","7"}))
cards=[4,5,6])
Card(children=[4,5]
title=Column(5)
label="Comparison"Quick comparison"
